391	</head>
392	<body>
393		<a class="skip-link" href="#main">Skip to content</a>
394		<header id="top">
395			<h1>Welcome</h1>
396			<nav aria-label="Page sections">
397				<ul>
398					<li><a href="#features">Features</a></li>
399					<li><a href="#examples">Examples</a></li>
400					<li><a href="#resources">Resources</a></li>
401				</ul>
402			</nav>
403		</header>
404		<main id="main" tabindex="-1">
405			<section aria-label="Introduction">
406				<p>This is a well-structured, accessible HTML5 document demonstrating modern best practices for semantic markup and inclusive design.</p>
407				<p>
408					It uses semantic landmarks, a skip link for keyboard navigation,
409					and CSS that adapts to your light or dark mode preference.
410				</p>
411				<p>
412					Text and link colors meet WCAG AA contrast in both themes, type scales
413					with your browser's font size, and motion respects your system settings.
414				</p>
415			</section>
416	
417			<section aria-labelledby="features">
418				<h2 id="features">Features</h2>
419				<ul>
420					<li>Semantic HTML structure with proper landmarks</li>
421					<li>Keyboard accessible navigation and focus management</li>
422					<li>Dark mode support with custom color schemes</li>
423					<li>Responsive typography using modern CSS</li>
424					<li>Print-friendly styles for better readability</li>
425					<li>WCAG AA contrast compliance in all color modes</li>
426				</ul>
427			</section>
428	
429			<section aria-labelledby="examples">
430				<h2 id="examples">Examples</h2>
431				<article class="card">
432					<h3>Component Cards</h3>
433					<p>Card components are useful for organizing related content. They include a subtle border and padding for visual separation.</p>
434					<a class="button" href="#resources">Learn more<span class="visually-hidden"> about accessibility resources</span></a>
435				</article>
436	
437				<article class="card">
438					<h3>Interactive Elements</h3>
439					<p>Buttons and links are fully accessible with clear focus states. All interactive elements include visible focus indicators and proper ARIA labels.</p>
440					<p><strong>Keyboard navigation:</strong> Use <kbd>Tab</kbd> to move forward, <kbd>Shift</kbd>+<kbd>Tab</kbd> to move backward, and <kbd>Enter</kbd> to activate.</p>
441				</article>
442	
443				<article class="card">
444					<h3>Accessible Form</h3>
445					<form id="contact-form" novalidate>
446						<p class="form-hint">Fields marked * are required.</p>
447						<div class="field">
448							<label for="email">Email <span aria-hidden="true">*</span></label>
449							<input type="email" id="email" name="email" autocomplete="email" spellcheck="false" autocapitalize="none" required aria-describedby="email-help">
450							<span id="email-error" class="error-message" role="alert"></span>
451							<small id="email-help" class="form-hint">For example, name@example.com</small>
452						</div>
453						<div class="field">
454							<label for="message">Message</label>
455							<textarea id="message" name="message" rows="4" maxlength="2000" aria-describedby="message-help"></textarea>
456							<small id="message-help" class="form-hint">Up to 2,000 characters.</small>
457						</div>
458						<button type="submit">Send message</button>
459						<p id="form-status" role="status"></p>
460					</form>
461				</article>
462	
463				<article class="card">
464					<h3>Live Region Example</h3>
465					<p>Click the button to announce a message using a live region. This demonstrates how screen readers are notified of dynamic updates.</p>
466					<button id="announce" type="button">Announce message</button>
467					<div class="live-region" aria-live="polite" aria-atomic="true">
468						<span id="live-message"></span>
469					</div>
470				</article>
471			</section>
472	
473			<section aria-labelledby="resources">
474				<h2 id="resources">Resources</h2>
475				<p>Want to learn more about web accessibility and semantic HTML? Check out these resources:</p>
476				<ul>
477					<li><a href="https://www.w3.org/WAI/WCAG22/quickref/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">WCAG 2.2 Quick Reference<span class="visually-hidden"> (opens in new tab)</span></a></li>
478					<li><a href="https://html.spec.whatwg.org/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">HTML Living Standard<span class="visually-hidden"> (opens in new tab)</span></a></li>
479					<li><a href="https://www.a11y-101.com/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">A11y 101<span class="visually-hidden"> (opens in new tab)</span></a></li>
480				</ul>
481			</section>
482		</main>
483		<footer>
484			<nav aria-label="Footer links">
485				<ul>
486					<li><a href="#top">Back to top</a></li>
487					<li><a href="https://github.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">GitHub<span class="visually-hidden"> (opens in new tab)</span></a></li>
488				</ul>
489			</nav>
490			<p><small>&copy; <time datetime="2026">2026</time>. All rights reserved.</small></p>
491		</footer>
492		<script>
493			const messages = [
494				"This update was announced to screen readers!",
495				"Dynamic content updates work with aria-live regions.",
496				"Live regions are essential for accessible web apps.",
497				"Try this with a screen reader like NVDA or JAWS!"
498			];
499			let nextMessage = 0;
500			const announceBtn = document.getElementById('announce');
501			const contactForm = document.getElementById('contact-form');
502			const emailInput = document.getElementById('email');
503			const formStatus = document.getElementById('form-status');
504	
505			if (announceBtn) {
506				announceBtn.addEventListener('click', () => {
507					document.getElementById('live-message').textContent = messages[nextMessage];
508					nextMessage = (nextMessage + 1) % messages.length;
509				});
510			}
511	
512			if (contactForm) {
513				const emailError = document.getElementById('email-error');
514	
515				const validateEmail = () => {
516					let message = '';
517					if (emailInput.validity.valueMissing) {
518						message = 'Enter your email address.';
519					} else if (!emailInput.validity.valid) {
520						message = 'Enter an email address in the format name@example.com.';
521					}
522					emailError.textContent = message;
523					if (message) {
524						emailInput.setAttribute('aria-invalid', 'true');
525						emailInput.setAttribute('aria-describedby', 'email-error email-help');
526					} else {
527						emailInput.removeAttribute('aria-invalid');
528						emailInput.setAttribute('aria-describedby', 'email-help');
529					}
530					return !message;
531				};
532	
533				emailInput.addEventListener('blur', () => {
534					if (emailInput.value || emailInput.hasAttribute('aria-invalid')) {
535						validateEmail();
536					}
537				});
538	
539				emailInput.addEventListener('input', () => {
540					if (emailInput.hasAttribute('aria-invalid')) {
541						validateEmail();
542					}
543				});
544	
545				contactForm.addEventListener('submit', (event) => {
546					event.preventDefault();
547					formStatus.textContent = '';
548					if (!validateEmail()) {
549						emailInput.focus();
550						return;
551					}
552					contactForm.reset();
553					emailError.textContent = '';
554					emailInput.removeAttribute('aria-invalid');
555					emailInput.setAttribute('aria-describedby', 'email-help');
556					setTimeout(() => {
557						formStatus.textContent = "Thanks! This is a demo, so nothing was sent.";
558					}, 100);
559				});
560			}
561		</script>
562	</body>
563	</html>
